course: dictionary
lesson: 15602
title: The tambourine
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tambourine is a musical instrument. It is a small round frame, a bit like a hand drum, with little metal discs called jingles around the edge. Musicians shake it or hit it to make a sound.
explain: The jingles are what make the tambourine special. When you shake it, they jingle, and when you tap it, they jingle too. «Mia shook the tambourine, and the jingles rang out.» The jingles give the instrument its bright, rattling sound.
explain: In music lessons, a tambourine is a percussion instrument. Percussion means instruments you hit, shake or scrape to keep the beat. «Let's tap the tambourine on every beat» means play it in time with the music.
fact: A tambourine is a musical instrument.
fact: It is a small round frame with metal discs called jingles around the edge.
fact: You can shake it or hit it to make a sound.
fact: Tambourines are used in school bands, folk music, church and gospel music, and pop songs.
fact: Useful phrases: «shake a tambourine», «tap the tambourine», «play the tambourine».
exercise: «Ravi shook the tambourine and the jingles rang out.» What are the jingles? | Bells sewn onto a shoe | The strings that hold the frame together | Small wooden drums inside the frame | *Little metal discs round the edge
exercise: «The class will tap the tambourine on every beat.» What does tap mean here? | Throw it across the room | Wrap it in a cloth to keep it dry | Put it away quietly on the shelf | *Hit it lightly so it makes a sound
exercise: What kind of instrument is a tambourine? | A keyboard with black and white keys | A string instrument with six strings | *A percussion instrument you shake or hit | A wind instrument you blow into
test: What are the little metal discs around a tambourine called? | Keys | *Jingles | Strings | Pedals
test: Which is a good way to keep the beat with a tambourine? | Blow hard into the frame | *Shake it or tap it in time with the music | Tie it to a chair | Leave it on the shelf until the end
exam: Which description best fits a tambourine? | A flat board with keys that you press | *A small round frame with jingles, shaken or tapped to keep the beat | A long wooden tube with holes that you blow into | A tall stick that you bang on the floor
